From: Steven Slivinski <stesli@microsoft.com>
Date: Tue, 5 May 2026 21:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gbm_wrapper: remap P010 -> P030 for BROADCOM SAND128 modifier

Mesa v3d (Raspberry Pi 5) only supports the BROADCOM SAND128 column-tiled
modifier with DRM_FORMAT_P030 (10-bit packed: 3 samples per 32-bit word),
not DRM_FORMAT_P010 (10-bit padded to 16). The chromium video pipeline
only knows viz::MultiPlaneFormat::kP010 which always maps to DRM_FORMAT_P010,
so we override the DRM format right at the gbm_bo_import call when we see
a BROADCOM-vendor modifier on a P010 buffer (the data layout is what
Mesa expects for P030; the only thing that needs to change is the fourcc
tag in the import descriptor).

Without this, gbm_bo_import returns NULL with:
  "Cannot create bo with format=(Y_UV, 420, 10unorm, ExtSamplerOn)"
in dmesg/Mesa logs, which prevents 10-bit HEVC frames from rendering.

---
 ui/gfx/linux/gbm_wrapper.cc | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/ui/gfx/linux/gbm_wrapper.cc
+++ b/ui/gfx/linux/gbm_wrapper.cc
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <gbm.h>
 #include <sys/mman.h>
 
+#include <drm_fourcc.h>
 #include <memory>
 #include <utility>
 #include <vector>
@@ -460,6 +461,22 @@
       UNSAFE_TODO(fd_data.offsets[i]) = handle.planes[i].offset;
     }
 
+    // PATCH_GBM_IMPORT_NC30: Mesa v3d (Pi 5) only accepts the BROADCOM
+    // SAND128 column-tiled modifier with DRM_FORMAT_P030 (10-bit packed:
+    // 3 samples per 32-bit word), not DRM_FORMAT_P010 (10-bit padded to
+    // 16). Chromium only knows kP010, so remap the fourcc tag here.
+#ifndef DRM_FORMAT_P030
+#define DRM_FORMAT_P030 fourcc_code('P', '0', '3', '0')
+#endif
+    constexpr uint64_t kBroadcomVendorShift = 56;
+    if (fd_data.format == DRM_FORMAT_P010 &&
+        (handle.modifier >> kBroadcomVendorShift) == 7 /* BROADCOM */) {
+      LOG(WARNING) << "PATCH_GBM_IMPORT_NC30: remapping P010 -> P030 for "
+                      "BROADCOM SAND128 modifier";
+      fd_data.format = DRM_FORMAT_P030;
+    }
+
     // PATCH_GBM_IMPORT_FIX diag: log handle/modifier/strides before import.
     {
       std::string sstr, ostr, fstr;
